 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Input:** A frame of TSDF volume data, represented as a sparse set of active voxel blocks. Each block contains $8 \times 8 \times 8$ voxels. A block is "active" if it contains at least one voxel with a valid TSDF value (i.e., within the truncation band).
-*   **Output:** A compressed bitstream representing the active blocks.
